module test.fixture.scaffold_disposition_census.pool_notes

data scaffold_disposition_census_fixture_pool_note: String = "Independently authored specimen pool for the exact scaffold disposition census (adhoc-220d7fd9-374, dashboard node). Every data declaration in the sibling pool/ directory is planted for a NAMED reason recorded as its own row in the sibling module expected_classification.dag -- the oracle is authored before any classifier exists, so its counts are a true oracle, not a measurement copied from the tree (DESIGN 'witness cost derives from purpose' / 'completeness is an identity join' rulings). Blocked: the census consumer itself is out of scope for this pool -- it is gated on the exact constructor/variant-value identity prerequisite in the decl_facts projection of data initializers (owned elsewhere), so nothing here decodes a Disposition value; the pool only has to exist and be well-formed. This note itself is deliberately homed OUTSIDE pool/, in this sibling module: pool/ is scanned wholesale by decl_facts(pool_roots) as the census subject universe, so a documentation-only String row living inside pool/ would itself become an undocumented real data declaration the oracle does not classify -- exactly the bug this file's extraction fixed. Section map: plain_int/plain_string/bare_construction_mechanism specimens are NonDisposition (unrelated types, or the Scaffold-arm payload type rather than Disposition itself). terminal_reason_a/b are Terminal, a genuine outcome distinct from ScaffoldDecodeRefused (the predecessor's bug folded every Terminal row into refusal by testing for exactly two positional children). scaffold_single_authority/realization_dispatch/substrate_mandatory_tag x whole/named specimens plus original_for_alias_specimen are ScaffoldDecoded, a full 3x2 cross of ConstructionMechanism x DeclField bind grain, each bind self-referential (module_path + own decl_name), matching the precedent already live in v2.std.decl_index's export_signature_facts_host_scaffold_dissolution_trigger; original_for_alias_specimen doubles as the aliasing target for aliased_disposition_specimen below. ScaffoldDecodeRefused has three distinct causes, none Terminal and none a clean Scaffold literal: aliased_disposition_specimen (cause 1, a bare reference to another data declaration rather than a Scaffold record literal), computed_disposition_specimen (cause 2, a call-expression initializer rather than a Scaffold record literal), and dangling_bind_target_specimen (cause 3, a well-formed Scaffold literal whose bind target does not exist anywhere in the pool -- the bind is dangling, not the initializer shape). plain_fn_specimen is an out-of-scope-by-kind control proving kind-based exclusion is decidable today without the blocked prerequisite (decl_facts already tags this ItemKind.FnItem, not ItemKind.DataItem); compute_disposition_specimen_value is the same control a second time."

data scaffold_disposition_census_decoys_note: String = "Two unrelated coproducts, one per file (pool/decoy_record.dag, pool/decoy_nullary.dag) because the compiler refuses two variants named Scaffold declared in the SAME module even across different types (a real, located, blocking diagnostic reproduced against decoys.dag before the split: variant Scaffold appears in both DecoyRecordDisposition and DecoyNullaryDisposition) -- so the adversarial pair is necessarily two modules, not one. One decoy spells a RECORD arm Scaffold { note: String }, the other a NULLARY arm Scaffold with no payload at all, covering both shapes a census could conflate with std.disposition.Scaffold (the nullary case matters distinctly: two nullary values of different types are otherwise indistinguishable by spelling alone). Neither module imports std.disposition -- under the current import-scoped resolver (DESIGN 'namespace-only name resolution', the '(today)' import-name-universe rule: own declarations union direct import lists) a bare Scaffold reference in either module can only resolve to that module's own local variant, never to std.disposition.Scaffold. This is the adversarial control that spelling is not type identity: a census that matches on the constructor lexeme Scaffold instead of the actual declared type Disposition would misclassify both specimens as ScaffoldDecoded."
